meta {
  name: S17 numbering
  seq: 18
}

docs {
  Story S17, TICK-664 (kit TICK-668, docs/acceptance/S17/README.md): release R1 of ADR-005, the counter key gets `scope_key` (migrations M1 and M2) and both allocation paths upsert on the 3-column key. Nothing changes for a user: every type keeps counting where it was. Needs the stack docs/acceptance/S17/tools/run-kit.sh prepares: a fresh stack on the pre-S17 build (S10 included) where tenant A's `incident` type is `gapless` and tenant B's is `gaps` (the default), each at INC0000042, then upgraded to the story build. One `INC` type per tenant (the prefix is unique per tenant), so the gaps type is tenant B's and Bob creates its incidents. AC1 (S17.6-S17.8): the first incident after the upgrade is INC0000043 on both. AC2 (S17.9-S17.10): 8 clients at once get unique numbers on both. Isolation, AC3 (S17.11-S17.14): Bob cannot read or change tenant A's INC0000043, and neither tenant's creates move the other's counter. Runs once per prepared stack: the exact numbers do not hold on a second pass.
}
